OPS = [
    ("Lead intake and qualification", "Account lead", "A new inquiry arrives by phone, referral, or web form.", "Capture the business problem before discussing tools. Separate verified facts from assumptions and do not promise a delivery date until capacity and dependencies are checked.", ["Record the contact, business type, requested outcome, urgency, budget range, decision-maker, and preferred follow-up channel.", "Ask what work repeats, who performs it today, what source material is used, and how the team will recognize a useful result.", "Classify the inquiry as discovery, qualified opportunity, or not-fit; explain the reason in neutral language."], "Save a dated CRM note with the prospect's own wording, unknowns, next action, and named owner.", "Escalate requests involving regulated advice, sensitive personal records, guaranteed business outcomes, or access to client systems before proposing scope."),
    ("Discovery call preparation", "Account lead", "A prospect accepts an introductory meeting.", "A discovery call is a short fact-finding conversation, not a technical proof or a promise that every requested feature exists. The goal is to understand one recurring workflow and decide whether a bounded pilot is appropriate.", ["Review only public company information and the prospect's volunteered context; do not collect personal records in advance.", "Prepare five questions about the current process, volume, handoffs, error cost, source documents, and approval owner.", "Send an agenda and state that the meeting will not include a production-data upload or a binding estimate."], "Record a summary, evidence, unresolved questions, and a yes/no/hold recommendation within one business day.", "Stop the conversation if the buyer expects legal, financial, insurance, medical, or safety advice from an AI system."),
    ("Workflow selection", "Operations lead", "The prospect names several possible use cases.", "Select one narrow workflow with frequent repetition, a stable source set, a human reviewer, and a measurable output. The workflow must be useful without granting the model authority to publish, spend money, or contact customers.", ["Map the request from trigger through inputs, decisions, output, reviewer, and final destination.", "Estimate examples per week and identify a baseline time or error measure using the prospect's own estimate.", "Choose the smallest task that can be tested with synthetic or approved low-risk material."], "Keep one signed workflow statement with scope, exclusions, success measure, and a named approver.", "Reject work that depends on undocumented judgment, broad system access, or an outcome that cannot be checked by a person."),
    ("Proposal and scope control", "Owner", "Discovery indicates a possible fit.", "The proposal must describe deliverables and boundaries in plain language. A price is not evidence that an untested capability is production-ready, and the proposal must not imply compliance certification or guaranteed accuracy.", ["List the chosen workflow, source set, user roles, included setup, acceptance tests, and delivery checkpoint.", "List exclusions such as automatic retrieval in every chat, self-service invitations, integrations, and unattended actions unless explicitly implemented and tested.", "State which model and embedding accounts the customer owns and pays for, along with the approved data path."], "Retain the dated proposal version and customer acceptance in the access-controlled account record.", "Do not begin paid setup until the scope, deposit, customer data owner, and provider billing responsibility are written down."),
    ("Customer onboarding and identity", "Deployment operator", "A signed pilot is ready for account setup.", "Public registration stays disabled. The customer names one owner and each employee receives a separate account. Gombey provisions accounts through the supported operator workflow until self-service invitations are implemented and tested.", ["Verify the requesting customer's authority using the agreed business contact, then record the approval without storing identity documents in chat.", "Create the owner account through the loopback-only bootstrap and immediately disable bootstrap registration.", "Create each member account individually, test sign-in, and share the approved knowledge agent with the USER role as Viewer."], "Keep the account roster, role, creation date, and revocation contact in the secured customer record.", "Pause if the customer requests shared passwords, open signup, or access for an unverified person."),
    ("Provider key ownership", "Customer admin", "A model or embedding provider is selected.", "The customer controls and funds its own provider account. A ChatGPT subscription is not an API key. Customer keys are entered only through the approved secret field or secret manager and are never pasted into chat or source control.", ["Explain separately where chat prompts and retrieved excerpts go and where source documents go for embedding.", "Have the customer create a limited, budget-capped provider credential with only the permissions needed for the pilot.", "Verify a small synthetic request, confirm which account is billed, and record provider name without recording the key."], "Record provider owner, model name, embedding provider, billing owner, and test timestamp; omit credential values.", "Stop if the only available key belongs to Gombey or if the customer cannot authorize the chosen provider's data handling terms."),
    ("Approved document intake", "Customer admin", "The team chooses documents for the shared assistant.", "Only documents approved by the customer owner for this purpose may be uploaded. Shared knowledge is attached to the Company Knowledge Assistant; an ordinary new chat does not automatically search that corpus.", ["Confirm owner, source, version, effective date, sensitivity, permitted audience, and whether the file contains personal or regulated data.", "Remove drafts, duplicates, secrets, unrelated personal data, and obsolete versions before upload.", "Upload the approved copy to the shared agent and test one known fact with a citation before inviting members."], "Keep a source register with filename, version, owner approval, upload date, and replacement or deletion date.", "Reject files without a clear right to use them or files that exceed the signed pilot's data category."),
    ("Knowledge-source change control", "Customer admin", "A policy, price, service, or process document changes.", "A shared assistant is only as current as its approved source set. Replacing a file does not authorize an undocumented policy change, and old versions should not remain retrievable unintentionally.", ["Identify the changed pages, effective date, owner, and downstream questions affected.", "Upload the approved version, remove or retire the superseded source, and wait for indexing to complete.", "Run the old-fact and new-fact regression questions and verify the citations point to the current source."], "Record old version, new version, change owner, test results, and completion time.", "Pause member use if two current-looking sources conflict or if the change affects a high-impact decision."),
    ("Project and file naming", "Project coordinator", "A new project or source file is created.", "Names should identify the client code, workflow, date, and version without putting sensitive personal data in a filename. A filename is an index, not an access-control boundary.", ["Use the pattern CLIENTCODE_workflow_YYYY-MM-DD_vNN_status.ext.", "Use the controlled client code rather than an individual's full name, account number, or confidential matter.", "Mark drafts, approved sources, and archived records consistently; do not reuse a version number for changed content."], "Store the naming convention in the project kickoff record and review it during the first source upload.", "Escalate any name that exposes a secret, personal identifier, or information the customer did not approve for the workspace."),
    ("Meeting notes and decisions", "Account lead", "A discovery, review, or delivery meeting ends.", "Notes must distinguish a decision from a suggestion. Do not record credentials, unnecessary personal details, or AI-generated claims as if a person verified them.", ["Capture attendees by role, date, decision, rationale, owner, due date, and open question.", "Read back material scope, price, timing, and data-handling decisions before closing the meeting.", "Send a concise recap through the approved business channel and invite corrections."], "Save the final recap in the controlled project folder and link it from the CRM record.", "Escalate a disputed price, unapproved scope change, or disagreement about who may authorize source data."),
    ("Brand asset authorization", "Creative director", "A client supplies a logo, photography, or brand guide.", "A supplied asset may be used only for the agreed work and channel. Possession of a file does not establish a license for every campaign or public use.", ["Record who supplied the asset, any license or usage window, required attribution, and approved channels.", "Check dimensions, color variants, accessibility contrast, and whether the asset includes a third-party mark.", "Keep original files unchanged and export working copies with an explicit version label."], "Maintain an asset register that links each approved file to its client, source, license note, and expiration date.", "Do not publish an asset when ownership, model release, music rights, or usage period is unclear."),
    ("Copy drafting and claims", "Copy lead", "A brief requires public-facing text.", "Drafts must be grounded in the approved brief and source material. Quantified, comparative, testimonial, environmental, health, and guaranteed-result claims require explicit evidence and client approval.", ["Extract only approved facts and label missing proof instead of filling gaps with plausible copy.", "Draft a version with a clear audience, benefit, offer, channel, and call to action.", "Use a claims checklist and route sensitive or comparative wording to the named client approver."], "Retain source links or document citations beside each material claim and preserve the approved final copy.", "Remove or flag claims that lack evidence; do not let an AI rewrite turn an estimate into a guarantee."),
    ("Design and accessibility review", "Design lead", "A visual asset is ready for review.", "Visual quality includes legibility and accessibility, not only brand appearance. A design preview must be checked at its intended size and must not imply a feature, product, or endorsement the client did not approve.", ["Check safe margins, text size, contrast, hierarchy, logo clear space, image rights, and crop at the target placement.", "Review the mobile view and a plain-text alternative for essential information.", "Compare the design against the approved brief and log each requested correction by page or frame."], "Store the approved source file, export dimensions, accessibility notes, reviewer, and final version.", "Hold delivery if critical offer terms are unreadable, a required disclaimer is missing, or a third-party asset is unlicensed."),
    ("Campaign schedule and dependencies", "Project coordinator", "A campaign has a target launch date.", "A launch date is a goal until dependencies are accepted. Schedule backwards from the date using review, revision, technical QA, and client approval buffers.", ["List copy, design, destination page, tracking, client review, legal or platform review, and access dependencies.", "Assign a responsible person and a due date to each item; identify a single final approver.", "Reforecast immediately when an input or approval misses its date; never silently compress QA."], "Keep a dated schedule with status, owner, dependency, and next checkpoint.", "Escalate a missed approval that leaves fewer than two business days for final QA; agree a revised date in writing."),
    ("Client approval and release", "Client approver", "A draft is proposed for publication or delivery.", "Only the named client approver can authorize public release. Internal review by Gombey is not client approval, and a thumbs-up on one asset does not approve unreviewed variants.", ["Send a numbered proof with channel, audience, date, offer, destination, and any factual claims visible.", "Request an explicit approval or an itemized correction list; resolve ambiguous replies before release.", "Check the approved version hash or filename against the final export before any authorized handoff."], "Record approver, timestamp, approved version, scope of approval, and any conditions.", "Do not publish, schedule, or send if approval is implied, partial, or attached to a different version."),
    ("Change request and revisions", "Project coordinator", "A client asks for work outside the approved brief.", "A revision corrects a deliverable within scope; a change request alters the audience, offer, channel, strategy, volume, or approved timeline. The distinction is documented before work begins.", ["Restate the request and identify which agreed deliverable or acceptance condition it affects.", "Estimate the schedule and cost effect, then obtain written client approval for the change.", "Update the versioned brief and dependencies before assigning production work."], "Keep the original request, impact note, approval, revised brief, and any price change together.", "Pause the affected work if the request conflicts with platform rules, a license, or a previously approved claim."),
    ("Landing-page content review", "Web producer", "A campaign directs users to a page or form.", "The destination must match the advertised offer and must explain eligibility, material limits, and next steps. Gombey does not submit or alter a client's production site without a separate written authorization.", ["Test the page on mobile and desktop, check the URL, form labels, keyboard path, and confirmation state.", "Verify offer amount, dates, eligibility, privacy link, contact route, and tracking consent language against the approved brief.", "Capture the final URL and a timestamped preview for the client approver."], "Record browser, device class, URL, form result, approved version, and any known limitation.", "Stop if the form collects unnecessary sensitive data or if the page's actual terms contradict the promotion."),
    ("Email campaign quality", "Email producer", "An approved email is ready for a customer list.", "Gombey may prepare a draft and checklist. The customer owns recipient consent, sending account, list hygiene, and final send authorization unless a separate tested integration is explicitly scoped.", ["Check sender identity, subject, preview text, links, merge fields, unsubscribe, and plain-text rendering.", "Send a synthetic test to an approved internal address and verify mobile rendering and destination URLs.", "Deliver the approved draft package to the customer; do not press send without explicit authorization and an available integration."], "Retain test recipient, rendering result, approved copy version, and client send decision.", "Hold if consent status is unknown, a list export is exposed, or any recipient field is unverified."),
    ("Social content and moderation", "Social lead", "A social post or reply is drafted.", "The customer retains account ownership and publishing authority. A draft must not imply that Gombey posted it, and replies involving complaints, safety, refunds, or personal information go to a human owner.", ["Check tone, caption, alt text, tag permissions, links, date, and the exact approved media variant.", "Provide a response suggestion only when the source and escalation path are known.", "Route account-specific disputes and personal messages to the client's designated human responder."], "Record status as draft, reviewed, approved, or customer-published; do not label a draft as live.", "Escalate threats, personal data, legal demands, platform enforcement, or a public safety concern immediately."),
    ("Analytics and KPI definitions", "Performance analyst", "A campaign metric is reported.", "Every KPI needs a defined numerator, denominator, date range, source, attribution rule, and data owner. Platform metrics from different sources should not be presented as interchangeable.", ["Write the metric formula before collecting results and note the reporting timezone.", "Use only customer-authorized exports or read-only access; exclude unrelated account data.", "Label estimates and attribution limits; compare against the stated baseline rather than an invented benchmark."], "Save a metric dictionary and report snapshot with date range, source, and caveats.", "Escalate missing or contradictory tracking; never claim causal lift from a simple before/after comparison without qualification."),
    ("Ad platform policy screening", "Campaign strategist", "A draft may be used in paid advertising.", "Platform rules change and eligibility depends on targeting, geography, product, and account status. A copy review is not a platform-policy certification or an ad account approval.", ["Identify the platform, geography, audience, destination, offer, and category restrictions.", "Check current official platform guidance before recommending a sensitive targeting choice.", "Mark uncertain claims for client review and keep a dated link to the applicable policy."], "Record platform, policy URL, review date, risk note, and customer approval owner.", "Do not promise ad acceptance, account reinstatement, reach, or conversion performance."),
    ("Vendor and contractor access", "Owner", "A contractor needs project access.", "Access is least-privilege, time-limited, and scoped to the customer's approved project. Sharing an account password is not an acceptable access method.", ["Confirm the project owner, requested task, data categories, and end date.", "Use a named account and the minimum access role available; avoid adding the contractor to unrelated projects.", "Revoke access at the end date and verify the contractor no longer appears in the roster."], "Record approver, named identity, role, scope, start, end, and revocation check.", "Pause when a vendor asks for shared credentials, an administrator role without need, or unapproved customer data."),
    ("Incident triage and escalation", "Operations lead", "A user reports a privacy, security, or availability incident.", "Preserve evidence and limit access before attempting repair. A support conversation is not an incident-response guarantee; material exposure is escalated to the customer owner promptly.", ["Record time, timezone, affected service, account, sanitized symptom, and business impact.", "Avoid copying customer prompts or documents into the ticket; secure necessary evidence under the agreed procedure.", "Contain the specific account, key, or service only under authorization, then identify the customer decision-maker."], "Maintain an incident timeline, containment action, owner, notification, and recovery evidence.", "Escalate suspected cross-user exposure, compromised credentials, unexpected public access, or unapproved provider use immediately."),
    ("Provider outage handling", "Operations lead", "A model or embeddings provider is unavailable or returns errors.", "A provider outage can interrupt model or retrieval behavior. The system must not silently invent a grounded answer after retrieval fails, and no switch to another provider occurs without customer approval.", ["Capture sanitized error, timestamp, provider, model, and whether the failure affects chat, embeddings, or both.", "Retry only within the documented safe limit and avoid uploading the same file repeatedly.", "Notify the customer and offer a non-AI fallback or a pause while the selected provider recovers."], "Record provider status, retry count, user impact, fallback, and recovery verification.", "Escalate repeated failures, duplicate charges, or any response that appears to claim retrieval succeeded when it did not."),
    ("Backup creation and custody", "Deployment operator", "A scheduled backup or pre-change backup is due.", "Backups contain customer data and secrets and must be encrypted. The recovery key is stored separately from the archive, and an archive is not considered useful until restore is tested.", ["Pause writers as documented and create the database, app-data, upload, and environment snapshots.", "Encrypt the archive and store it in the customer-approved destination with restricted access.", "Verify checksums and manifest without exposing document bodies or secrets."], "Record backup timestamp, versions, destination reference, checksum, retention date, and key-custody reference.", "Do not place an unencrypted customer backup or its recovery key on a general-purpose external drive."),
    ("Restore rehearsal", "Deployment operator", "A backup is introduced or a recovery drill is scheduled.", "Restore only into a fresh isolated project. Never test recovery over the active deployment or a second customer's volumes.", ["Create a clean project with unique network and storage identifiers.", "Restore each database and file component, apply the intended secrets, and check the service health route.", "Verify one synthetic account, approved agent, source citation, and deletion behavior; then remove the disposable restore only after evidence is recorded."], "Keep restore start/end, archive identifiers, components, test cases, and cleanup confirmation.", "Stop if the restore points to production volumes or if the encryption key is missing or unverified."),
    ("Member offboarding", "Customer admin", "The customer requests removal of a member.", "The customer confirms the identity and authority for the request. Removing a member account does not automatically delete that member's historical records or backup copies.", ["Verify the request with the authorized customer admin using the agreed channel.", "Disable the account using the supported procedure and test that sign-in is denied.", "Review ownership of personal files and the customer's retention instruction before deleting data."], "Record requester, account identifier, action time, sign-in denial, and retention decision.", "Escalate a disputed request, legal hold, or unclear ownership of a shared source before deletion."),
    ("Forgotten-password recovery", "Deployment operator", "A member cannot sign in and requests a reset.", "Public email reset remains disabled until secure email is configured and tested. The operator verifies the request, uses the interactive hidden prompt, and delivers the temporary password through an approved secure channel.", ["Verify the member and request through the customer's admin or agreed support channel.", "Run the pinned app's supported reset command over the approved operator session; never pass a password in shell history.", "Confirm the affected member can sign in and that the password-version change invalidated old sessions."], "Record verification and completion without writing the password into a ticket or shared notes.", "Do not reset an account based only on an unverified email or a message from another employee."),
    ("Data retention and deletion", "Customer admin", "A file, account, or deployment reaches its retention date.", "Deletion scope includes active app records, indexes, files, and later backup expiration. Do not promise immediate erasure of retained encrypted backups unless the agreed retention procedure supports it.", ["Identify the exact customer, file version, vector scope, and instruction authorizing deletion.", "Remove the active source through the supported path and confirm the retrieval no longer returns its unique synthetic marker.", "Track the separate backup-expiry date and document what is retained until that date."], "Keep a deletion record with scope, timestamp, verification, and backup-retention end date.", "Pause deletion if the request conflicts with a hold, export request, or another customer's shared source."),
    ("Support boundaries and response targets", "Account lead", "A customer asks for help or an urgent guarantee.", "A response-time target means acknowledgment in the agreed period, not a guaranteed fix time or uptime level. Provider outages, new features, and out-of-scope work are separately estimated.", ["Collect a sanitized symptom, affected workflow, impact, time, recent changes, and workaround.", "Acknowledge within the signed target and state who owns the next update.", "Estimate resolution and any out-of-scope work before making changes or exceeding support allowance."], "Track severity, acknowledgment time, next update, support time, and customer-approved work.", "Escalate a suspected security issue immediately; do not promise round-the-clock coverage unless contracted."),
    ("Delivery acceptance", "Owner and customer approver", "The agreed setup has reached its delivery checkpoint.", "Acceptance is tied to agreed tests, not a subjective claim that the model is perfect. A failed test is documented, scoped, and either fixed or explicitly accepted as a limitation.", ["Run the signed account, shared-source, privacy, provider billing, and workflow questions.", "Review each result against the stated expected answer and identify any retrieval miss or unsupported assertion.", "Collect written acceptance or a dated issue list and agree the next corrective step."], "Store the completed acceptance record, software versions, known limitations, and customer sign-off.", "Do not mark delivery complete while a data-isolation test or a required critical workflow check is unresolved."),
    ("Renewal and cancellation", "Owner", "A monthly service term is approaching renewal or a customer asks to stop.", "The recurring service begins on the contractually agreed date, with explicit customer consent and a valid payment method. Cancellation and data export timing are explained before the first recurring charge.", ["Check the signed plan, start date, amount, launch term, tax treatment, and saved-payment consent.", "Notify the customer of the next charge date and how to cancel through the approved payment channel.", "At cancellation, follow the agreed data export, access removal, backup retention, and DNS steps."], "Retain consent evidence, invoice/renewal status, cancellation request, and offboarding checklist.", "Do not activate a recurring charge from a one-time setup payment without clear customer consent."),
]


